WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.068
-Hello, everyone,

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:06.039
and welcome to "Late Night"
from my hallway.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.874
As I'm sure you all know,
our show is dark,

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:10.510
our staff is all at home,
and we have no idea

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.379
when we're going to be back,
but obviously

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:14.080
it's not just a surreal time
for us,

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.815
it's a surreal time
for everyone.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.349
We're all trying to process it,

00:00:17.349 --> 00:00:19.085
so we thought we'd start
doing that

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.487
the way we always do,
with "A Closer Look."

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:24.824
Now, you might notice that
I'm doing this "Closer Look"

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.826
from inside my house,
and it may be weird

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.961
to do it from a hallway,

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:34.133
but at least I'm not doing it
from a public beach!

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.835
Look at those dummies.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.503
Let me be clear.

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:39.605
I'm not saying people are dumb
for going to the beach

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:41.307
during a pandemic,
which they are.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:44.377
I'm saying you're for going
to the beach, period.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:47.046
You could die from going
to a beach right now,

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:49.548
and it's still not in
the top five worst things

00:00:49.548 --> 00:00:51.217
that can happen to you
at a beach.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:54.387
When I die, I fully expect
my last words to be,

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:56.489
"At least I don't have
to go to the beach anymore."

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:59.292
I mean, I'm not happy
being stuck inside all the time,

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:03.229
but at least I'm not finding
sand in my butt crack -- yet.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.031
Anyway, "Late Night's"
in quarantine

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.633
but we're still processing
a public health crisis,

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:10.770
economic crisis, crisis of
leadership at the federal level.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.005
There's a lot to process,
so for more on this,

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:15.274
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:19.378
♪♪

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:21.580
The stock market plummeted
again this morning,

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:23.916
and the number of coronavirus
cases across the world

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:28.221
has now surpassed 300,000,

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:30.490
with about 40,000
here in the U.S.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:33.625
Or as the president assured us
at the start of this crisis...

00:01:33.625 --> 00:01:35.295
-When you have 15 people,

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:37.263
and the 15 within
a couple of days

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.532
is going to be down to
close to zero...

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:43.236
-Ah! So close.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:46.138
Trump's like the dumbest "Price
is Right" contestant in history.

00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:47.973
"Donald, how much for this
brand-new Porsche,

00:01:47.973 --> 00:01:49.675
dining set,
and 10-day luxury stay

00:01:49.675 --> 00:01:52.411
at the Ritz-Carlton in Hawaii?
-Close to zero.

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:55.881
[ "Price is Right"
horn plays ]

00:01:55.881 --> 00:01:58.518
-"Does the horn sound
mean I won?

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:01.120
Was that the winner's horn?"

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.122
I really hope people remember
that comment

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:05.725
as we watch a pandemic overwhelm
our health care system

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:08.628
and wreck our economy
while we sit on our couches

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:11.330
scrolling all the way
to the bottom of Netflix

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:12.932
looking for something new
to watch?

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:15.401
"Honey, look, look, honey.
Honey, I found a documentary

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:16.635
called, let me see,

00:02:16.635 --> 00:02:18.470
'Secret Wildcats
of the Scottish Highlands.'

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.106
I don't think we've seen
that one yet, honey.

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:21.807
No, we watched it last night

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:26.179
and the secret is,
it's a boring documentary."

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:28.214
Because while the federal
government could have been

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:31.817
ramping up testing, tracing,
and quarantining cases

00:02:31.817 --> 00:02:33.819
and containing the spread,
the president was lying

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:36.588
and claiming this was all
no big deal.

00:02:36.588 --> 00:02:38.891
In fact, we now know,
thanks to new reporting

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:43.028
in the "Washington Post,"
that U.S. intelligence agencies

00:02:43.028 --> 00:02:45.231
were issuing ominous
classified warnings

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:47.633
in January and February
about the global danger

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:50.069
posed by the coronavirus,
while President Trump

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:51.971
and lawmakers played down
the threat

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.505
and failed to take action.

00:02:53.505 --> 00:02:56.642
So either he knew about it
the whole time and lied,

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:58.745
or he wasn't paying attention
during his briefings,

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:02.047
and honestly, both are
probably true.

00:03:02.047 --> 00:03:03.549
Donald Trump cannot stand

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:05.251
when someone else
is talking in a meeting.

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.886
I mean, look at him.

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:09.388
He literally looks down
at the table

00:03:09.388 --> 00:03:11.724
and hugs himself like he's
hoping it's all a dream.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.526
Pretty soon he's just going
to start going to meetings

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:16.796
wearing a, I don't know,
a ThunderShirt?

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:19.165
But of course, we can't expect
Trump to actually

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.900
read one of his intelligence
briefings

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.302
unless Sean Hannity
holds it up to the screen

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:24.970
during his show.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.807
In fact, the "Post" reported
that Trump's advisers

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:30.476
struggled to get him
to take the virus seriously.

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:33.746
Health Secretary Alex Azar
couldn't get through to Trump

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:37.049
to speak with him about
the virus until January 18th,

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:38.685
when he reached Trump by phone.

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:42.021
The president interjected
to ask about vaping

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:45.090
and when flavored vaping
products would be

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:46.892
back on the market.

00:03:46.892 --> 00:03:51.563
He was more concerned
about vaping than coronavirus.

00:03:51.563 --> 00:03:53.833
He is a 16-year-old
high school burnout

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:56.535
trapped in a 70-year-old
retiree's body.

00:03:56.535 --> 00:04:00.172
Our hospitals might run out
of masks and ventilators,

00:04:00.172 --> 00:04:02.041
but at least Trump will
still make sure

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.743
they have plenty of
Peppermint E-Juice.

00:04:04.743 --> 00:04:07.246
"Smoke this.
It'll make the pain stop.

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:10.550
Or it won't. There's no science
behind any of this."

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.752
And now, partially because
of Trump's negligence,

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:15.154
over 100 million Americans,
nearly a third of the country,

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:17.056
are under stay-home orders.

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:19.892
Basically it's like a cross
between a staycation

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.560
and a "Saw" movie.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.662
Now the situation
is grim and surreal,

00:04:23.662 --> 00:04:25.365
but that doesn't mean
there haven't been

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:27.933
moments of positivity,
like those penguins

00:04:27.933 --> 00:04:29.535
who are let loose
in the aquarium

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.304
and allowed to gawk
at the other animals,

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:33.172
finally allowing them
to be as snooty

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:35.908
as the tuxedos nature
provided them.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:38.243
"Look at the riffraff
in their casual wear.

00:04:38.243 --> 00:04:42.247
This is an aquarium,
not an above-ground pool."

00:04:42.247 --> 00:04:45.485
Or Steve Martin playing
his banjo in, I don't know,

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:48.554
I guess the middle of the woods.

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:51.190
And you know things are bad
when the sound of someone

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.859
playing a banjo in the woods
is comforting.

00:04:53.859 --> 00:04:56.461
Usually that's when you run
back to the camper

00:04:56.461 --> 00:04:58.163
and head for the city.

00:04:58.163 --> 00:05:02.234
I will say, "Deliverance"
would have been a whole

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:04.637
entirely different movie

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:07.607
if it had been Steve Martin
instead of that weird kid.

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:08.774
"How was your camping trip?"

00:05:08.774 --> 00:05:10.409
"You know what?
It was hilarious.

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:11.877
It was so funny.

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:13.179
It was so funny
even when someone

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:16.315
got shot through the head
with an arrow.

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:19.285
Now, countries across the world
have taken drastic measures

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:21.354
to slow the spread
of the pandemic by, quote,

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:24.156
"flattening the curve,"
which sounds like

00:05:24.156 --> 00:05:27.393
something a CrossFit instructor
would yell during a workout.

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.695
"Come on, Janet!

00:05:29.695 --> 00:05:34.733
Janet, let's finish those squats
and flatten those curves!"

00:05:34.733 --> 00:05:37.803
But it basically just means
slowing the spread out

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:41.373
over a longer period time,
rather than having one big spike

00:05:41.373 --> 00:05:44.076
that overwhelms the health care
system all at once.

00:05:44.076 --> 00:05:47.113
European governments
from France to Italy to Spain

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:50.216
have all taken extreme measures
to lock down their countries

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:52.284
and slow the spread
of the disease,

00:05:52.284 --> 00:05:55.821
and in Germany, even
Chancellor Angela Merkel

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:58.891
was apparently getting ready
when she was photographed

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:01.694
over the weekend
at her local supermarket

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:05.198
buying four bottles of wine
and some toilet paper.

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:07.366
Either she's preparing
to self-quarantine,

00:06:07.366 --> 00:06:10.569
or she's about to get hammered
and TP the principal's house.

00:06:10.569 --> 00:06:12.538
[ German accent ]
"Take that, Mr. Himmelschmitt!

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:16.676
Oh, I just the saw the light!
Go! Run! Schnell! Schnell!"

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:20.245
And drastic measures
are already having

00:06:20.245 --> 00:06:23.282
a major impact on economic
activity across the world.

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:25.284
"The Financial Times"
reported on Sunday

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:28.454
that road traffic has always
fallen in most major cities.

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:31.023
Rome, Paris, and New York
have all seen rush-hour traffic

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:34.460
running at considerably below
their usual average levels.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:37.296
Rush-hour traffic has fallen
in New York.

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:41.400
And in New York, all traffic
is rush-hour traffic.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:42.935
Every hour is rush hour.

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:45.171
If someone gets a flat tire
in Queens,

00:06:45.171 --> 00:06:48.840
the whole Eastern Seaboard
locks up for three hours.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.344
If you try and catch a cab
in Midtown at rush hour,

00:06:51.344 --> 00:06:53.512
you'd be better off just
ordering all the parts

00:06:53.512 --> 00:06:55.514
and building your own cab.

00:06:55.514 --> 00:06:57.750
Order them from rockauto.com,

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:00.052
which is a commercials
a lot of writers

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:01.320
on our staff enjoy.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.122
And yet, there are still
some people who don't seem

00:07:03.122 --> 00:07:04.590
to be taking the situation
seriously,

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.826
particularly young people
who are still crowding

00:07:06.826 --> 00:07:08.160
beaches and parks.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.663
So over the weekend,
New York Governor Andrew Cuomo

00:07:10.663 --> 00:07:11.997
had a message for them.

00:07:11.997 --> 00:07:14.332
-We do have an issue
with younger people

00:07:14.332 --> 00:07:15.667
who are not complying.

00:07:15.667 --> 00:07:17.669
You want to have an opinion?
Have an opinion.

00:07:17.669 --> 00:07:19.805
But you can't have
your own facts.

00:07:19.805 --> 00:07:23.409
"Well, young people don't
get this disease."

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:26.978
You are wrong.
You can get this virus.

00:07:26.978 --> 00:07:31.150
And you can transfer
the virus.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:36.088
Social distancing works,

00:07:36.088 --> 00:07:40.926
and you need social distancing
everywhere.

00:07:40.926 --> 00:07:42.828
There's a significant
amounts of noncompliance,

00:07:42.828 --> 00:07:47.099
especially in New York City,
especially in the parks.

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:48.667
I'm going to go down there
today.

00:07:48.667 --> 00:07:51.337
I want to see what
the situation is myself.

00:07:51.337 --> 00:07:53.138
-Yo, [bleep]

00:07:53.138 --> 00:07:55.440
If you guys don't stay
at least 6 feet apart,

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:58.977
Andrew Cuomo will
turn this car around right now!

00:07:58.977 --> 00:08:01.313
He's gonna go down to the parks
himself and bust some skulls,

00:08:01.313 --> 00:08:03.582
and he's gonna bring
his brother Chris with him.

00:08:03.582 --> 00:08:05.384
Look at these guys.
Not only are they

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:07.720
gonna enforce social distancing,
they're gonna

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:10.823
hang you upside down
and steal your lunch money.

00:08:10.823 --> 00:08:13.992
Seriously, I would watch
an entire after-school special

00:08:13.992 --> 00:08:18.598
with an undercover Andrew Cuomo
posing as a teen skateboarder,

00:08:18.598 --> 00:08:22.234
you know, trying to bust kids
for hanging out in the park.

00:08:22.234 --> 00:08:24.303
"Pot is cool.
You know what else is cool?

00:08:24.303 --> 00:08:26.639
Staying inside
and reading books."

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:29.641
Also I love that one of
the slides in his presentation

00:08:29.641 --> 00:08:34.479
literally said, "Young people,
you are wrong."

00:08:34.479 --> 00:08:36.882
That is serious big dad energy.

00:08:36.882 --> 00:08:39.684
"You were wrong. Now go
to your room for two months.

00:08:39.684 --> 00:08:41.019
Think about what you did.

00:08:41.019 --> 00:08:43.822
Better hear you
washing your hands in there."

00:08:43.822 --> 00:08:46.391
So the coronavirus pandemic
has impacted

00:08:46.391 --> 00:08:48.427
virtually every aspect
of society,

00:08:48.427 --> 00:08:51.731
from Hollywood to sports
to politics.

00:08:51.731 --> 00:08:53.866
Just yesterday we found out
that Rand Paul

00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:57.069
was the first senator
diagnosed with coronavirus.

00:08:57.069 --> 00:08:59.371
Thankfully his office says
that he's feeling fine,

00:08:59.371 --> 00:09:00.906
and that's great news.

00:09:00.906 --> 00:09:02.541
Now we could point out
the fact that Paul

00:09:02.541 --> 00:09:04.309
was the only senator to vote
against the bipartisan

00:09:04.309 --> 00:09:05.944
coronavirus aid package,

00:09:05.944 --> 00:09:08.647
or the fact that he stood
by an incompetent president

00:09:08.647 --> 00:09:11.050
who botched the response
to this crisis

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:13.418
and called criticism
of his response a hoax.

00:09:13.418 --> 00:09:16.322
But I want to focus on this
part of the story.

00:09:16.322 --> 00:09:18.657
-Out of an abundance of caution,
Senator Paul,

00:09:18.657 --> 00:09:20.492
despite the fact
he did not have symptoms,

00:09:20.492 --> 00:09:24.696
decided to get tested
about six or seven days ago

00:09:24.696 --> 00:09:27.800
So what we're learning is that
in that time frame,

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:30.702
those six or seven days
since he got tested,

00:09:30.702 --> 00:09:34.606
he has been up on Capitol Hill
attending GOP lunches.

00:09:34.606 --> 00:09:37.076
He also,
as we reported earlier today,

00:09:37.076 --> 00:09:39.345
was spotted at the Senate gym.

00:09:39.345 --> 00:09:43.582
-Senator Rand Paul tests
positive for coronavirus,

00:09:43.582 --> 00:09:45.851
and fellow lawmakers
spotted him

00:09:45.851 --> 00:09:48.721
in the Senate swimming pool
earlier today.

00:09:48.721 --> 00:09:51.757
-So Rand Paul thought
he might have coronavirus,

00:09:51.757 --> 00:09:54.593
and he went to the gym
and the pool.

00:09:54.593 --> 00:09:57.363
What else did he do, lick every
desk in the Senate chamber

00:09:57.363 --> 00:09:59.832
and shake hands with
the Lincoln Memorial?

00:09:59.832 --> 00:10:02.268
Also of course he goes
to the Senate pool.

00:10:02.268 --> 00:10:04.369
That explains his hair.

00:10:04.369 --> 00:10:07.906
Dude, wear a swimming cap.

00:10:07.906 --> 00:10:09.475
Or maybe that is.

00:10:09.475 --> 00:10:12.445
Is that a swimming cap?

00:10:12.445 --> 00:10:14.079
Seriously, if you think you
have coronavirus,

00:10:14.079 --> 00:10:16.248
you're supposed to stay home,
not go to the gym.

00:10:16.248 --> 00:10:18.851
Coronavirus doesn't care
if you're jacked.

00:10:18.851 --> 00:10:21.387
I mean, Idris Elba got it,
and look at him.

00:10:21.387 --> 00:10:23.388
If anyone's capable
of knocking out coronavirus

00:10:23.388 --> 00:10:26.792
by punching it,
it's Idris Elba.

00:10:26.792 --> 00:10:29.094
And now several other
Republican senators

00:10:29.094 --> 00:10:30.829
have been forced
to self-quarantine,

00:10:30.829 --> 00:10:33.632
including Utah Senator
Mitt Romney.

00:10:33.632 --> 00:10:36.134
Trump, who's feuded with Romney,
apparently found out

00:10:36.134 --> 00:10:38.737
about that fact in real time
during his daily

00:10:38.737 --> 00:10:41.207
coronavirus reality show
on Sunday night,

00:10:41.207 --> 00:10:44.276
and deployed his trademark
charm and compassion.

00:10:44.276 --> 00:10:46.479
-On top of Senator Paul,
now four senators

00:10:46.479 --> 00:10:49.581
are in isolation,
and the rules say that they

00:10:49.581 --> 00:10:51.016
were going to vote --
-Who are they, please?

00:10:51.016 --> 00:10:53.652
Who are they?
-Mitt Romney, Senator Lee...

00:10:53.652 --> 00:10:55.320
-Senator Gardner...
-Senator Gardner.

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:57.322
-...and Rick Scott
-Senator Rick Scott also.

00:10:57.322 --> 00:10:58.657
Two of them were in contact --

00:10:58.657 --> 00:11:00.559
-Well, I guess Rick
is coming out.

00:11:00.559 --> 00:11:02.894
-With the critical stimulus
package vote expected --

00:11:02.894 --> 00:11:04.763
-Romney's in isolation?
-Yes.

00:11:04.763 --> 00:11:07.633
-Gee, that's too bad.
Go ahead.

00:11:07.633 --> 00:11:11.369
-Do I detect sarcasm there, sir?
-No, no, none whatsoever.

00:11:11.369 --> 00:11:13.905
-"No, no"?
Oh, that wasn't sarcasm?

00:11:13.905 --> 00:11:16.341
So you're genuinely,
genuinely concerned

00:11:16.341 --> 00:11:17.877
about Romney's well-being?

00:11:17.877 --> 00:11:20.412
Did you also send him
a get-well card that said,

00:11:20.412 --> 00:11:24.216
"Oh, you're so sick?
I'm<i> so</i> sorry."

00:11:24.216 --> 00:11:26.551
That's just a reminder that
Donald Trump never passes up

00:11:26.551 --> 00:11:30.423
an opportunity to remind us
that he is an awful person,

00:11:30.423 --> 00:11:33.225
even in the midst
of a global pandemic.

00:11:33.225 --> 00:11:34.960
It's almost like he's afraid
we'll forget.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:37.229
Like, he's worried
that if he's too focused

00:11:37.229 --> 00:11:39.698
on solving the crisis,
people won't remember

00:11:39.698 --> 00:11:42.401
he's also the same ass [bleep]
who once tweeted,

00:11:42.401 --> 00:11:45.804
"I have never seen a thin person
drinking Diet Coke."

00:11:45.804 --> 00:11:48.340
In fact, last night after
yet another rambling,

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:50.810
self-absorbed performance,
Trump, who just recently

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:53.112
called himself
a "wartime president,"

00:11:53.112 --> 00:11:55.648
took to Twitter to complain
about press coverage

00:11:55.648 --> 00:11:57.783
of his disastrous
coronavirus response.

00:11:57.783 --> 00:12:00.419
"I watch and listen
to the fake news CNN,

00:12:00.419 --> 00:12:05.424
MSDNC, ABC, NBC, CBS,
some of Fox desperately,

00:12:05.424 --> 00:12:07.927
foolishly pleading
to be politically correct,

00:12:07.927 --> 00:12:10.229
'The New York Times'
and 'Washington Post,'

00:12:10.229 --> 00:12:12.531
and all I see is hatred of me
at any cost.

00:12:12.531 --> 00:12:16.669
Don't they understand that they
are destroying themselves?"

00:12:16.669 --> 00:12:19.571
How do you have time
to watch six networks

00:12:19.571 --> 00:12:21.707
and read two newspapers?

00:12:21.707 --> 00:12:23.808
I've been home with two kids
for a week, and the only thing

00:12:23.808 --> 00:12:26.545
I've read is the back of a box
of Clorox Wipes

00:12:26.545 --> 00:12:28.881
and the only thing I've watched
is my wife roll her eyes at me

00:12:28.881 --> 00:12:31.450
for not knowing how to
make oatmeal.

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:33.118
Trump thinks he's
a wartime president because

00:12:33.118 --> 00:12:36.054
anytime someone asks him
a question, he's like,

00:12:36.054 --> 00:12:38.991
"Okay, it's wartime."

00:12:38.991 --> 00:12:41.259
If you want to be a wartime
president, you can't tweet

00:12:41.259 --> 00:12:43.262
petty complaints
about the media.

00:12:43.262 --> 00:12:46.065
Churchill never started
any of his speeches by saying,

00:12:46.065 --> 00:12:47.900
"We shall fight them
on the beaches.

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:50.736
"We shall fight them
on the landing ground.

00:12:50.736 --> 00:12:53.272
Even though the fake news
will never give me credit."

00:12:53.272 --> 00:12:57.009
My voice coach has been
unavailable,

00:12:57.009 --> 00:12:59.177
in case you're wondering why
that Churchill was so bad.

00:12:59.177 --> 00:13:01.313
We're in this crisis in part --

00:13:01.313 --> 00:13:04.483
He's not sick or anything,
he's just doing other stuff.

00:13:04.483 --> 00:13:05.951
We're in this crisis in part

00:13:05.951 --> 00:13:07.786
because of the authoritarian
cult of personality

00:13:07.786 --> 00:13:08.954
that surrounds our president.

00:13:08.954 --> 00:13:10.189
Instead of facing
the stark truth,

00:13:10.189 --> 00:13:11.957
Trump demands constant
praise and flattery.

00:13:11.957 --> 00:13:13.959
In fact, at one point
last week,

00:13:13.959 --> 00:13:16.729
a reporter simply tried to ask
Trump about the very real,

00:13:16.729 --> 00:13:19.564
urgent concerns faced by
health care professionals

00:13:19.564 --> 00:13:21.767
on the front lines about
the lack of medical equipment

00:13:21.767 --> 00:13:23.735
like masks and ventilators.

00:13:23.735 --> 00:13:26.171
Things are so bad
TV medical dramas

00:13:26.171 --> 00:13:27.839
have been donating their
medical supplies

00:13:27.839 --> 00:13:31.610
to hospitals in need
during the coronavirus panic.

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:33.512
That's right, our government
is such a mess,

00:13:33.512 --> 00:13:35.714
TV shows have had to pitch in
by giving every hospital

00:13:35.714 --> 00:13:37.416
in the country masks,
ventilators,

00:13:37.416 --> 00:13:40.652
and one super hot doctor who
gets killed off in season 11.

00:13:40.652 --> 00:13:42.588
"Don't get too close
to the cute doctor.

00:13:42.588 --> 00:13:44.489
They never last.

00:13:44.489 --> 00:13:46.491
They never do."

00:13:46.491 --> 00:13:48.527
So Trump was asked about
those concerns

00:13:48.527 --> 00:13:51.763
at one of his press conferences,
and this was his response.

00:13:51.763 --> 00:13:53.465
-I just want to read you
some of what some of

00:13:53.465 --> 00:13:56.468
the doctors on the front lines
of this crisis are saying.

00:13:56.468 --> 00:13:57.770
Doctor --
-You mean the ones that are

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.371
saying good things
or bad things?

00:13:59.371 --> 00:14:01.973
-I assure you, no one
who is saying good things

00:14:01.973 --> 00:14:03.475
is a medical professional.

00:14:03.475 --> 00:14:05.477
You think in the middle of
a global pandemic

00:14:05.477 --> 00:14:07.212
that's overwhelming
our health care system

00:14:07.212 --> 00:14:08.880
and triggering
an economic collapse

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:10.448
a reporter's gonna raise
their hands and say,

00:14:10.448 --> 00:14:12.317
"Mr. President,
I want to read you

00:14:12.317 --> 00:14:15.087
some of the beautiful tributes
that are pouring in"?

00:14:15.087 --> 00:14:16.655
Seriously, why are you
like this?

00:14:16.655 --> 00:14:18.757
Why do you have
the emotional maturity

00:14:18.757 --> 00:14:20.759
of a middle school student
passing a note in class

00:14:20.759 --> 00:14:25.531
that says, "Do you like me?
Check yes or yes"?

00:14:25.531 --> 00:14:27.266
Now, on top of botching
a public health crisis,

00:14:27.266 --> 00:14:28.901
Trump and his Republican
allies in Congress

00:14:28.901 --> 00:14:31.336
are also trying to ram through
a stimulus package

00:14:31.336 --> 00:14:33.005
they negotiated
with themselves

00:14:33.005 --> 00:14:35.674
as the economy craters
and millions of vulnerable

00:14:35.674 --> 00:14:37.442
working Americans miss out
on their paychecks

00:14:37.442 --> 00:14:39.811
and struggle to make it
through the crisis.

00:14:39.811 --> 00:14:41.914
Trump and his allies want
to shovel bailout money

00:14:41.914 --> 00:14:44.482
into the pockets of corporations
without any strings attached.

00:14:44.482 --> 00:14:48.820
They've also proposed
a one-time $1,000 check

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.789
to Americans struggling
through the crisis.

00:14:50.789 --> 00:14:53.425
During a live stream yesterday,
Senator Bernie Sanders,

00:14:53.425 --> 00:14:57.162
who's called for monthly
payments of $2,000

00:14:57.162 --> 00:14:58.930
said that wasn't nearly
enough.

00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:02.000
-I know some of my Republican
colleagues are talking about,

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:05.570
gee, a one-time $1,000 payment.

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:08.106
Really? Really?

00:15:08.106 --> 00:15:10.242
Yeah, that will last you
for two or three weeks,

00:15:10.242 --> 00:15:12.211
and what happens after that?

00:15:12.211 --> 00:15:15.213
-Okay, first of all,
"Really?" is my segment, Bernie.

00:15:15.213 --> 00:15:16.715
You don't see me going around

00:15:16.715 --> 00:15:19.018
blasting millionaires
and billionaires.

00:15:19.018 --> 00:15:21.854
Okay, actually, yeah, no,
I have done that.

00:15:21.854 --> 00:15:23.756
All right, we're even.
Second, he's right.

00:15:23.756 --> 00:15:26.024
A one-time check for 1,000 bucks
is not even close

00:15:26.024 --> 00:15:27.392
to what we need.

00:15:27.392 --> 00:15:28.560
What's Trump gonna
propose next,

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:30.162
free vaping products?

00:15:30.162 --> 00:15:33.532
"To help with the pandemic,
we'll be sending every American

00:15:33.532 --> 00:15:37.603
a monthly supply of
cucumber flavored Juul pods.

00:15:37.603 --> 00:15:40.839
Smoke 'em before your lungs
are filled with coronavirus."

00:15:40.839 --> 00:15:42.441
Instead of bailing out
big corporations

00:15:42.441 --> 00:15:44.409
with no strings attached,
maybe we can bail out

00:15:44.409 --> 00:15:47.479
the American people instead
by just giving them money.

00:15:47.479 --> 00:15:50.115
Besides, if you send a check
to the airlines,

00:15:50.115 --> 00:15:51.750
there's a good chance
it'll just get mixed up

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:54.319
with someone else's check
and end up in the wrong airport.

00:15:54.319 --> 00:15:56.321
Why do cruises need a bailout

00:15:56.321 --> 00:15:58.223
before workers
or rural hospitals?

00:15:58.223 --> 00:15:59.725
No one wants to see Goofy
walking around

00:15:59.725 --> 00:16:02.427
the deck of a Disney cruise
holding two bags of cash

00:16:02.427 --> 00:16:04.229
and smoking a Juul.

00:16:04.229 --> 00:16:05.564
Mm.

00:16:05.564 --> 00:16:07.266
All right, I kind of
want to see it.

00:16:07.266 --> 00:16:09.968
At this point it's become clear
that to get through this crisis

00:16:09.968 --> 00:16:11.803
we're gonna have to rely
on state and local governments,

00:16:11.803 --> 00:16:13.238
our courageous
health care workers,

00:16:13.238 --> 00:16:15.240
our public health experts,
and each other

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:17.276
because when it comes to Trump,
the chances

00:16:17.276 --> 00:16:19.143
he'll provide real leadership
are...

00:16:19.143 --> 00:16:20.411
-Close to zero.

00:16:20.411 --> 00:16:22.013
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:16:22.013 --> 00:16:25.917
♪♪

00:16:25.917 --> 00:16:27.953
We will see you soon.

00:16:27.953 --> 00:16:30.989
Stay safe. Wash your hands,
and remember --

00:16:30.989 --> 00:16:33.559
the beach sucks.

